<h1 class="sectionedit1" id="eci">ECI</h1>
<div class="level1">

</div>



        <h2 style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 150);">Important note</h2>

        <div style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 150);">
          <p>
            Most of ECI's original goals have been achieved, and currently there is not a lot of activity anymore inside ECI. All of the resources developed in the past are nonetheless still provided on this web site. Any remaining activities are currently being carried out on two Google groups:
          </br></br>            <a href="https://groups.google.com/g/eci-de">https://groups.google.com/g/eci-de</a>
          </br></br>            <a href="https://groups.google.com/g/eci-en">https://groups.google.com/g/eci-en </a>
          </br></br>            
            This site will not be updated frequently.
          </p>
        </div>






<h2 class="sectionedit2" id="european_color_initiative_eci">European Color Initiative (ECI)</h2>
<div class="level2">

<p>
The European Color Initiative (ECI) is a group of experts, working on device independent processing of color data in digital publication systems. ECI has been founded in June 1996 in Hamburg at the initiative of the publishing houses Bauer, Burda, Gruner+Jahr and Springer.
</p>

</div>

<h2 class="sectionedit3" id="recent_news">Recent news:</h2>
<div class="level2">

</div>

<h3 class="sectionedit4" id="profile_for_metal-printing_offset_fogra60">Profile for »Metal-Printing (offset) – (FOGRA60)«</h3>
<div class="level3">

<p>
<em>Berlin, January 26 2022:</em> For the printing condition »Metal-Printing on white coated metal 1 (MPC1)« ECI provides a profile named “Metal-Printing_MPC1_FOGRA60.icc” based on the Fogra colour characterization data set FOGRA60. <a href="doku.php_id=en_colorstandards_offset.html" class="wikilink1" title="en:colorstandards:offset" data-wiki-id="en:colorstandards:offset">Please click here for further information</a>.<em> [2022-01-26 |::| FSu]</em>
</p>

</div>

<h3 class="sectionedit5" id="profile_ecicmyk_v2_for_the_updated_cmyk_exchange_color_space_fogra59_available">Profile »eciCMYK v2« for the updated CMYK exchange color space »FOGRA59« available</h3>
<div class="level3">

<p>
<em>Berlin, July 05, 2021:</em> The updated version “eciCMYK v2” provides an enhanced gray axis and extends the field of application of the CMYK exchange color space compared to it’s predecessor. <a href="doku.php_id=en_colourstandards_workingcolorspaces.html#ecicmyk_fogra53_cmyk_exchange_color_space" class="urlextern" title="doku.php_id=en_colourstandards_workingcolorspaces.html#ecicmyk_fogra53_cmyk_exchange_color_space" rel="ugc nofollow">Information about the new CMYK color exchange space is available here</a>. The profile <a href="doku.php_id=en_downloads.html#eci_profiles_current_versions" class="urlextern" title="doku.php_id=en_downloads.html#eci_profiles_current_versions" rel="ugc nofollow">»eciCMYK v2« is available in the download section</a>.<em> [2021-07-05 |::| FSu]</em>
</p>

</div>

<h3 class="sectionedit6" id="eci_realeases_supplement_surface_finishing_for_pso_coated_v3">ECI releases Supplement »Surface finishing for PSO Coated v3«</h3>
<div class="level3">

<p>
<em>Berlin, October 30, 2020:</em> The ECI provides profiles for „PSO Coated v3“ prints with matte and glossy lamination.  <a href="doku.php_id=en_colorstandards_offset.html" class="wikilink1" title="en:colorstandards:offset" data-wiki-id="en:colorstandards:offset">Please click here for further information</a>.<em> [2020-10-30 |::| FSu]</em>
</p>

</div>

<h3 class="sectionedit7" id="psr_v2_update_of_gravure_profiles">»PSR_V2« update of gravure profiles</h3>
<div class="level3">

<p>
<em>Berlin, February 05, 2020:</em> Following feedback from the market, the profile PSR_LWC_PLUS_V2_M1.icc published in December 2019 was renamed to PSR_LWC_PLUS_V2_M1<strong>_v2</strong>.icc for unique identification. The identifier “_v2.icc” marks the difference between the new profile and the profile published in 2018: the new profile was created with the new software version of the Heidelberg ColorToolbox, so that all profiles of the PSR V2 M1 family are uniform.<em> [2020-02-05 |::| TH/FSu]</em>
</p>

</div>

<h3 class="sectionedit8" id="psr_v2_gravure_profiles_for_all_papers_available">»PSR_V2« gravure profiles for all papers available</h3>
<div class="level3">

<p>
<em>Berlin, December 22, 2019:</em> After 10 years it is time for an update. From now on all gravure profiles PSR V2 for the measurement condition M1 are available for download. Information about the new profiles can be found under <a href="http://www.eci.org/en/colourstandards/gravure" class="urlextern" title="http://www.eci.org/en/colourstandards/gravure" rel="ugc nofollow">more information about »PSR LWC plus v2 M1«</a>. You can download the complete update profile package with the necessary documentation, application recommendations and characterization data from the <a href="http://www.eci.org/en/downloads?&amp;#eci_offset_profiles_current_versions" class="urlextern" title="http://www.eci.org/en/downloads?&amp;#eci_offset_profiles_current_versions" rel="ugc nofollow">download area</a> as a ZIP archive.
Some proofing system manufacturers offer color adaptations that contain optimizations that are not provided in ICC technology, e.g. simulation of printing behavior (noise), multiple iterations, etc. These special adaptations and corresponding support are also available for updates directly from the respective proofing system manufacturer.
</p>

</div>

<h3 class="sectionedit9" id="update_of_the_psr_v2_gravure_profile_for_lwc-plus_paper_available">Update of the »PSR_V2« gravure profile for »LWC-Plus« paper available</h3>
<div class="level3">

<p>
<em>Berlin, March 09, 2018:</em> The update of the PSR V2 gravure profile for LWC-Plus paper is available for immediate download. The Update of the profile has been extended to include the necessary documentation, usage recommendations and characterisation data. Click here for <a href="http://www.eci.org/en/colourstandards/gravure" class="urlextern" title="http://www.eci.org/en/colourstandards/gravure" rel="ugc nofollow">more information about »PSR LWC plus v2 M1«</a>. The new profile along with the characterization data and further information is  <a href="http://www.eci.org/en/downloads?&amp;#eci_offset_profiles_current_versions" class="urlextern" title="http://www.eci.org/en/downloads?&amp;#eci_offset_profiles_current_versions" rel="ugc nofollow">available for immediate download here as a ZIP archive</a>.
</p>

<p>
Some proofing system manufacturers offer colour adaptations which include optimisations which are not available in the ICC process model, such as simulation of print behaviour (noise), multiple iterations etc. These special adaptations and their support are available directly from the relevant proofing system supplier.<em> [2018-03-09 |::| TH/FSu]</em>
</p>

</div>

<h3 class="sectionedit10" id="profile_ecicmyk_for_the_cmyk_exchange_color_space_fogra53_available">Profile »eciCMYK« for the CMYK exchange color space »FOGRA53« available</h3>
<div class="level3">

<p>
<em>Berlin, August 28, 2017:</em> The CMYK exchange color space »FOGRA53« has been developed in light of the Fogra research project 10.057, aimed at developing tools for a media neutral print workflow. The respective ECI profile »eciCMYK« is <a href="http://www.eci.org/en/downloads#exchange_color_space_ecicmyk" class="urlextern" title="http://www.eci.org/en/downloads#exchange_color_space_ecicmyk" rel="ugc nofollow">available for download immediately</a>, along with device link profiles for the conversion to »PSO Coated v3« and »PSO Uncoated v3« and from »ISO Coated v2«. Click here for <a href="http://www.eci.org/en/colourstandards/workingcolorspaces" class="urlextern" title="http://www.eci.org/en/colourstandards/workingcolorspaces" rel="ugc nofollow">more information about eciCMYK and FOGRA53</a>.
</p>

<p>
The new characterization data set FOGRA53 is <a href="https://www.fogra.org/en/fogra-standardization/fogra-characterizationdata/a-icc-en.html" class="urlextern" title="https://www.fogra.org/en/fogra-standardization/fogra-characterizationdata/a-icc-en.html" rel="ugc nofollow">available for download on the Fogra website</a>. The ECI profile eciCMYK is <a href="http://www.eci.org/_media/downloads/icc_profiles_from_eci/ecicmyk.zip" class="urlextern" title="http://www.eci.org/_medi